638→Demonstrates setting the up vector (@up) attribute to control orientation of geometry. The up vector is first set using the set() function, then shown using inline vector syntax. Finally, the up vector is animated by using sin(@Time) for the x-component, making the orientation change over time based on the global Time attribute.
639→
640→### Rotating Up Vector with Time [[Ep6, 47:36](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yPaWl3AiSrc&t=2856s)]
641→```vex
642→v@up = set(sin(@Time), 0, cos(@Time));
