737→This snippet demonstrates multiple unrelated operations: calculating distance from origin, creating a color vector based on distance and an offset parameter, setting an up vector using sine and cosine, and modifying Y position with a sine wave. The code appears to be a collection of examples rather than a cohesive algorithm, possibly from end-of-lesson exercises.
738→
739→### Animated up vector using distance and time [[Ep6, 56:52](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yPaWl3AiSrc&t=3412s)]
